PLANS

This folder holds one plan per work phase of this repository's project.
A phase covers a range of versions; ROADMAP.md lists the milestones and
their version numbers, and each plan says how to reach them.


NAMING

  P<n>-<name>.md, numbered in the order the phases run, for example
  P1-foundation.md for 0.0.x. IN THIS REPOSITORY, below, lists the
  plans with their version ranges.

  Numbers are never reused. A new phase gets the next number, even when
  it runs between two existing ones; its version range says where it
  fits.


WHAT A PLAN HOLDS

  Status        not started, in progress, or done, with the current
                version
  Goal          what the phase achieves, in a sentence or two
  Versions      each version in the phase with its work items
  Acceptance    the checks that say a version is done
  Dependencies  what the phase adds or removes (keep
                arch/dependencies.md in step)
  Risks         what could go wrong, and what we do about it
  Open points   questions for Fred, which stay open until he decides


KEEPING PLANS CURRENT

  - Update the status line when work starts and when a version lands.
  - When the work shows a plan was wrong, change the plan in the same
    commit as the code, and say why in the commit message.
  - Fred's decisions are written into the plan as decisions, with their
    date. Until then, a remark from Fred is context, not a decision.
  - Bugs found while working on a phase go in bugs/, linked from the
    plan.


IN THIS REPOSITORY

  P1 through P31 hold the product and feature plans migrated from
  docs/plans/ (including P1 for 0.6.x, P2 for 1.0.0, P3 for 1.1-1.3).
  P32-early-releases.md covers 0.4.8-0.5.12; P33-northern-torch.md
  covers the 0.7.x Northern Torch phases and 17-milestone breakdown.
  Historical Gate A / 0.4.x filing cards sit read-only in work/history/.
  Product behavior and generic defaults belong here; exact assemblies
  belong in tamlinux-packages; personal selections belong in user config.
